---
source: crates/poly-mcp/tests/surface.rs
expression: instructions
---
poly lints and formats every language with one config. Tools: `check` (no writes), `fix` (writes), `info` (read-only state), `manage` (cache and components). `check`/`fix` run the tools the repository's poly.toml configures: use them only on repositories you trust. Results are the CLI's `--format json` document plus a `poly` block naming the binary that answered. `isError` means the run did not verify what was asked: a file failed, a requested phase did not run, or nothing ran at all, which is `{error: {kind, message}, summary: null}` (invalid or inapplicable arguments are `kind: usage`). Findings and drift are not errors. Gate on `summary.checked`, not on an empty `results`: a clean file has no record. Whole-project scopes and component downloads return a Task when the client supports them; poll tasks/get. Output schemas: resources under poly://schema/.
